  )
  (text "POWER\nUSB-C in, 5V. The two 5.1k resistors on CC tell the charger to send 5V.\nUse a 5V 3A USB-C supply: the LED grid can pull a lot of current (firmware caps brightness).\n+5V   = digital 5V and LEDs (straight from USB through the fuse)\n+5VA  = quiet 5V for the YM2612 and the audio circuit (through a ferrite bead)\nVSYS  = feeds the Pico through a diode, so plugging USB into the Pico for\n        programming and the main USB-C at the same time is safe\n+3V3  = made by the regulator on the Pico board (see Controller page)\nAll grounds are one net. On protoboard, run the audio ground and the LED ground\nas separate wires back to the USB-C connector (star ground)." (at 25.4 25.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 77054184-cd8a-5dd9-bc0f-9ef1304d7748)
  )
)
